    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nThe code for buffer text object should be `col = math.max(vim.fn.getline('$'):len(), 1)` rather than `col = vim.fn.getline('$'):len()`. One example is correct but the one in the `Examples` section is missing the call to `math.max`.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.0-dev\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `help mini.ai`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNo selection is done if the last line is empty.",
